($t$Jasminum grandiflorum$t$, $t$Jasminum grandiflorum$t$, $t$Oleaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Oleaceae. Portamento: Climber. Altezza massima indicativa: 2.5 m. Jasminum grandiflorum, also known as Jasmin, White fragrant flower, or Spanish Jasmine among others, is an evergreen or deciduous shrub growing about 2-4 m tall. It has opposite, pinnate leaves comprised of 5-11 leaflets and white fragrant flowers. There are two recognized subspecies: J. grandiflorum subs. floribundum and S. grandiflorum subs. grandiflorum. It is widely cultivated as an ornamental plant. Flowering commence at 6 months after planting. Jasmin is highly valued for its very fragrant flowers which are source of essential oil used in perfumery. The oil also has medicinal uses specifically as a muscle relaxant and an aphrodisiac. Moreover, Jasmin flowers are used for coughs, headache, weak eyes, scorpion stings, and skin diseases. It is also a popular flavoring in tea. The leaves are used against ulcers.$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Jasmin$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Oleaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto